        "title": {
          "en": "Research Identifies Causal Explanations for LLM Jailbreaks",
          "zh": "大型语言模型越狱：新研究探究其因果机制"
        },
        "tl_dr": {
          "en": "New research investigates why safety-trained large language models can be induced to answer harmful requests through jailbreak prompts.",
          "zh": "一项新研究正深入探讨经过安全训练的大型语言模型为何仍能被越狱提示诱导，从而响应有害请求。"
        },
        "key_takeaways": {
          "en": [
            "The research paper is identified as arXiv:2605.00123v1, announced as a new publication.",
            "It focuses on why safety-trained large language models (LLMs) can often be induced to generate harmful responses via jailbreak prompts.",
            "Previous studies have explored jailbreak success by analyzing LLM's intermediate representations."
          ],
          "zh": [
            "该研究论文的标识符为 arXiv:2605.00123v1，且被标注为“新发布”类型。",
            "研究核心在于理解已接受安全训练的LLM如何被越狱提示引诱，以生成有害回复。",
            "此前研究曾通过分析模型中间表示，来探究越狱成功的机制。"
          ]
        },
        "impact": {
          "en": "A lack of understanding regarding LLM susceptibility to jailbreaks means future autonomous models operating in high-stakes environments may also be vulnerable to such attacks. This research aims to address that fundamental challenge.",
          "zh": "由于对LLM易受越狱攻击的原因缺乏深入理解，未来在更高风险场景中自主运行的尖端模型也可能面临类似威胁。本研究旨在应对这一核心挑战。"
        },
        "source": "arXiv CS.AI",
        "link": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.00123"
      },
